"For positive integers $\\Delta$ and $t$, let $h_t(\\Delta)$ be the smallest integer such that every graph $G$ with at least $h_t(\\Delta)$ edges and maximum degree $\\Delta(G)\\le \\Delta$ contains two edges at distance at least $t$. **Cambie–Cames van Batenburg–Joannis de Verclos–Kang conjecture.** For $t\\ge 3$ and every $\\varepsilon>0$,\n\n$$\nh_t(\\Delta)\\le (1+\\varepsilon)\\Delta^t\n$$\n\nfor all sufficiently large $\\Delta$. This is an asymptotic strengthening of the known general upper bound of order $\\frac32\\Delta^t$. It remains open according to the supplied paper context."